<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-11--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch05-11: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.20";
    dc:description "This is an explicit suspicion about a future identification between some network system and spacetime, with no accompanying prediction. Precision data on gravity and particle physics can confirm or refute particular models that make particular predictions. They do not contain a variable corresponding to 'some of these systems will in the end turn out to be closely related,' so the claim as stated has no discriminating test.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The claim suspects that some network systems will turn out to be closely related to the structure of space and spacetime. No network rule, no derived continuum limit, and no observation that would fail if the suspicion were wrong are identified.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'Closely related' can be satisfied by any discrete model that recovers ordinary geometry at large scales, or withdrawn if that model fails, without touching the suspicion.", "Tests of Lorentz invariance or of general relativity constrain specific discrete-spacetime proposals, not an unspecified future network system.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.8"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.195"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch05-11--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of wolfram2002-ch05-11 by Grok 4.7: 0.2";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.2"^^xsd:double;
